# What `docker build` must NOT send to the Docker daemon.
#
# The Dockerfile already uses an allow-list (`COPY *.py ./`), so none of this
# could reach the image anyway. This file solves the other half of the problem:
# everything here is uploaded as "build context" before the first instruction
# runs. Without it, every build ships venv/ (62 MB) and — more to the point —
# .env and gcreds.json to the daemon for no reason at all.
#
# Result: a build context of a few hundred KB, and secrets that only ever arrive
# the way they should — as the read-only bind mounts in docker-compose.yml.

# Secrets. Mounted at run time, never built in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.client.example
gcreds.json
*.json

# Local Python environment — the image installs its own from
# requirements.docker.txt, and a Mac venv would not work on Linux regardless.
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Live data. The SQLite database is a bind mount to ./data on the host; copying
# a Mac-side copy into the build would be a stale snapshot at best.
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite3

# Editor/OS noise and the snapshots taken before edits.
*.py.bak.*
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
.DS_Store

# Tunnel identity. Mounted read-only into the cloudflared container.
cloudflared/

# Docs and git history are not needed to run the agent.
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
